TIMSAC Modern Fortran is an independent and unofficial modern Fortran port of
the numerical core of the R package timsac 1.3.8-6.

Original package authors and contributors include:

  Yoshinori Kawasaki
  Junji Nakano
  Masami Saga
  The Institute of Statistical Mathematics

The original TIMSAC program package was developed by members of the Institute
of Statistical Mathematics, including Hirotugu Akaike. Individual legacy
source files retain credits for their designers and programmers where those
credits appeared in the source package.

Original files are copyright (C) 2005 The Institute of Statistical
Mathematics. See reference/COPYRIGHTS and reference/DESCRIPTION for the
retained original notices and package metadata.

